**Structure (11 sections, 3 theory beats, 3 [theory→widgets] pairs):**
1. theory `po-co-onnx` — ONNX as exchange format, opset as ABI
2. codeCloze `export-cloze` — `torch.onnx.export` with opset/const-folding slots
3. dataTable `ep-table` — ONNX Runtime EPs comparison (CPU/CUDA/TensorRT/OpenVINO/DML/CoreML/ROCm)
4. theory `fp16-int8-theory` — FP16/BF16/INT8 layout, PTQ vs QAT, with IEEE 754 image
5. code `int8-quantizer-code` — symmetric INT8 quantize/dequantize in NumPy (4 tests, solution)
6. plotImage `latency-vs-map-plot` — FP32/FP16/INT8 latency + mAP@0.5 (PNG rendered to `assets/plots/…-1.png`)
7. quiz `int8-pitfalls-quiz` — multi-select INT8 calibration pitfalls
8. theory `domain-specific-eval` — PSNR/ENL/EPI, mIoU, mAP + per-incidence-angle, with Sentinel-1 SAR image
9. code `enl-epi-code` — ENL & EPI in NumPy (4 tests, solution)
10. dragMatch `metric-task-match` — metric ↔ task pipeline mapping
11. sandbox `ptq-sandbox` — per-tensor vs per-channel PTQ exploration
Lesson-level `sources`: 6 entries (PyTorch ONNX docs, ONNX Runtime perf, PyTorch Quantization, Mixed Precision Training paper, COCO eval protocol, PSNR/ENL/EPI critical review). Section-level sources on each of the 3 theory beats and on the int8 code section. No files written under `scripts/ralph/`.
